; TYPED key domains on an open struct-map rest row (`* K => V` where `K` is not bare
; `uint`/`text`/`any`). These rows take the seek path: the loop body hoists a `raw.position()`
; anchor, a declared-key match arm that falls through rewinds to it, and `K::deserialize` reads the
; key itself — so the write and read halves are the same `K` codec, symmetric by construction.
; Snapshotted in the plain, preserve, json and wasm flavors. Under the json flags a typed rest key
; images through the `any` domain's convention applied to `K`'s OWN CBOR bytes — the rows below cover
; both emitted routes (a NOMINAL K reads its head at runtime; a PRIMITIVE K states its image
; directly), including the two shapes with no member-name image at all (`bytes`, whose JSON face is a
; pure error surface). The VALUE-level vectors live in `tests/open-struct-map-json-e2e`.
md = int / bytes / text

; Local union K crossed with BOTH declared key kinds: the uint arm and the text arm each get a
; rewinding catch-all, and a declared key never reaches `Md::deserialize` (declared keys peel first).
union_rest = {
  1: uint,
  "nm": text,
  * md => uint
}

; Sidecar-bearing K: under --preserve-encodings a `bytes` key contributes a `StringEncoding` to
; `rest_key_encodings`, bound by the key's own deserialize rather than by a peek.
bytes_rest = { 1: uint, * bytes => text }

; Sized-int K (`u8`): the uint arm's catch-all rewinds and re-reads through the bounds check, so a
; key outside the u8 range is a parse error rather than a silent capture. `Option<Sz>` sidecar.
sized_rest = { 1: uint, * uint .size 1 => uint }

; Encoding-op K: the peeked path never saw the tag, so `* #6.24(uint) => v` used to write a tag its
; deserialize never read. On the typed path the tag rides `K`'s own codec in both directions.
tagged_rest = { 2: uint, * #6.24(uint) => uint }

; Typed K under `@duplicates preserve`: the PairMap twin, whose keys need only the `ord` demand.
dup_rest = {
  9: uint,
  * md => text ; @duplicates preserve
}
